The separation metrics of dimensionality-reduction evaluation can count each group once: `evaluate_embedding(sample_weight="group")`, or `"sample_weight": "group"` in an eval spec, weights the scaling, the fit and the balanced accuracy so that each class weighs the same and, within a class, each group the same, however many samples it has there. By default each sample counts once, as before. The random forest uses 200 trees instead of 300, 1.5 times faster with the same scores within its seed-to-seed spread.
